# Convex conventions

- Public `query`/`mutation`/`action` must declare `args` and `returns` validators.
- Await every promise (`ctx.db.*`, `ctx.scheduler.*`, `ctx.run*`).
- Use `.withIndex()` instead of `.filter()`; add the index to `convex/schema.ts`.
- Avoid unbounded `.collect()`; paginate or `.take(n)` anything that can grow.
- No `Date.now()` / `new Date()` inside queries; pass time in as an argument or use mutations/crons.
- Only schedule or `ctx.run*` `internal.*` functions, never `api.*`.
- Seats are identified by per-tab `clientId`. Validate with `assertValidClientId` (`lib/session.ts`) and authorize room actions with `requirePlayer` (`lib/roomAuth.ts`).
- Accounts are optional: read the signed-in user with `optionalAccount` / `requireAccount` (`lib/auth.ts`, backed by `ctx.auth`), never from a client-supplied argument. Credential data (`accounts`, `authSessions`, `authAttempts`) is only touched by internal functions in `authStore.ts`; public functions return whitelisted fields via explicit `returns` validators.
- Keep function wrappers thin; game logic lives in `lib/` (`lib/game/*`, `lib/gameStore.ts`).
- `"use node"` files may only export actions.
- No `any`; use `Doc<"table">` / `Id<"table">` from `_generated/dataModel`.
